From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2-mem2mem: Let a driver run the next job at once

A job finished schedules the next on the system workqueue, as the
caller may be atomic. A driver that finishes its jobs in a threaded
interrupt handler can sleep, yet its device idles until a worker wakes:
on an RK3528 decoding at 3840x2160, 40 to 60 us a frame.

Add v4l2_m2m_run_next(), which runs the next queued job in the
caller's context, as v4l2_m2m_resume() already does. The scheduled
work still runs and finds the job running.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c |  7 +++++++
 include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h           | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
index a65cbb1..66fd21a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
@@ -541,6 +541,13 @@ unlock:
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish);
 
+void v4l2_m2m_run_next(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev)
+{
+	might_sleep();
+	v4l2_m2m_try_run(m2m_dev);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(v4l2_m2m_run_next);
+
 void v4l2_m2m_suspend(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev)
 {
 	unsigned long flags;
diff --git a/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h b/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h
index 31de25d..84af910 100644
--- a/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h
+++ b/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h
@@ -313,6 +313,18 @@ v4l2_m2m_is_last_draining_src_buf(struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx,
 void v4l2_m2m_last_buffer_done(struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx,
 			       struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *vbuf);
 
+/**
+ * v4l2_m2m_run_next() - run the next queued job now
+ *
+ * @m2m_dev: opaque pointer to the internal data to handle M2M context
+ *
+ * Called after v4l2_m2m_job_finish() or v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish()
+ * from a context that can sleep, such as a threaded interrupt handler, it
+ * starts the next job without waiting for the workqueue those schedule. The
+ * work still runs, and finds the job already running.
+ */
+void v4l2_m2m_run_next(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev);
+
 /**
  * v4l2_m2m_suspend() - stop new jobs from being run and wait for current job
  * to finish
